    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem of arranging 3 math books and 5 English books on a shelf where all the math books must stay together and all the English books must also stay together, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Treat the Groups of Books as Single Units:**\n   Since we need to combine the math books into one unit and the English books into another unit, we are dealing with two groups. Thus, we can consider each combination separately.\n\n2. **Arranging the Groups:**\n   First, determine the number of ways to arrange these two groups on the shelf.\n   - There are 2 positions where we can place the groups - top and bottom of the shelf or left and right.\n   - The number of permutations of 2 groups is \\(2!\\). Hence, there are \\(2!\\) ways to arrange the groups.\n   \\[\n   2! = 2 \\times 1 = 2\n   \\]\n   The permutations are:\n   - Math group first, English group second\n   - English group first, Math group second\n\n3. **Arranging Books Within each Group:**\n   Next, we need to arrange the books within each group.\n\n   - For the Math group:\n     There are 3 math books, and they can be arranged among themselves in:\n     \\[\n     3! = 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 6\n     \\]\n   arrangements.\n\n   - For the English group:\n     There are 5 English books, and they can be arranged among themselves in:\n     \\[\n     5! = 5 \\times 4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 120\n     \\]\n     arrangements.\n\n4. **Combining All Arrangements:**\n   The total number of arrangements when both groups are indistinguishable is given by the product of the number of permutations for each group.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total arrangements} = 2 \\times 3! \\times 5!\n   \\]\n\n   Now calculate the product of these values:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times (3!) \\times (5!) = 2 \\times 6 \\times 120 = 1440\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of ways to arrange the 3 math books and 5 English books on the shelf, considering that the math books must stay together and the English books must stay together, is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1440}\n\\]",
